<<<
The difference is that, while o.t. can be either adjectival or adverbial (The accident was not o. t. carelessness; O.t. my carelessness he broke his leg), d.t. can only be adjectival (The accident was not d.t. carelessness).
===
The difference is that, while *o. t.* can be either adjectival or adverbial (*The accident was not o. t. carelessness; O. t. my carelessness he broke his leg*), *d. t.* can only be adjectival (*The accident was not d. t. carelessness*).
>>>

